-- title:
--   Zeros of ̄ j - j₀ count the degree over ℚ̄(̄ j)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive natural number and let $F$ denote `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((X))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((X))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions `divisorExpansions N`; let `jBar N` be the element of $F$ given by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq`. Let $j_0 \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\,$`jBar N`$\,)$ obtained by adjoining `jBar N`. Let $S$ be a finite set of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a place being a valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring, with $\operatorname{ord}_v$ the negative logarithm of its associated adic valuation — and suppose that $S$ consists exactly of those places $v$ with $\operatorname{ord}_v(\,$`jBar N`$\, - j_0) > 0$. Then $\sum_{v \in S} \operatorname{ord}_v(\,$`jBar N`$\, - j_0)$ equals the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\,$`jBar N`$\,)$-dimension of $F$.
--
--   This is the standard count of the zeros of a nonconstant function on a curve with multiplicity, applied to $\bar j - j_0$ on the modular curve of level $N$: the total order of vanishing above $j_0$ equals the degree of the map to the $j$-line. It supplies the numerical input for the description of the places of the level-$N$ modular function field lying above a given $j$-invariant, and is used in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_finset_forall_exists_sp_eq_forall_inertia_smul_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_finset_forall_exists_sp_eq_forall_inertia_smul_eq).
